{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J5"],
      "pins": ["J5.1", "J5.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/Microcontroller/HEATER"],
      "observed": "The netlist places screw terminal J5 directly on the MCU heater-control net: J5 pin 2 is on /Microcontroller/HEATER (also ESP32 GPIO1 and TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN), and J5 pin 1 is on GND.",
      "expected": "The specification describes only J6 as the heater connector driven by U6 OUT; it does not include an external screw terminal on the GPIO1/U6 control net. A connector on this net should not be present unless intended as a documented manual override/input with proper protection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"4\") (name \"/Microcontroller/HEATER\") ... (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Closing or wiring J5 can short the heater-control line to ground, overriding firmware heater control and potentially causing ESP32 GPIO1 output contention; an external voltage applied to J5 could also reach GPIO1 and U6 IN/DIAG_EN without protection.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most connectivity and values match the specification, but screw terminal J5 is connected between GND and the MCU/U6 heater-control net, which is not described in the intended design and could override or damage the heater control path if used."
}

